    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change rejects a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400 response.\n\n**What I did:** In `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, I added a Bean Validation constraint to the `registrationDate` property of the `OwnerFields` schema:\n\n```yaml\nx-field-extra-annotation: \"@jakarta.validation.constraints.PastOrPresent\"\n```\n\n**Why this approach:** Per the project's Spring conventions, this is the idiomatic path and mirrors the existing pattern already used for the `telephone` field (which applies its own validator via `x-field-extra-annotation`). The generator emits `@PastOrPresent` onto the generated `OwnerFieldsDto.registrationDate` (a `LocalDate`). When a future date is supplied, `@Valid` on the controller body triggers a `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, which the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` already maps to **400 Bad Request**. Omitted (`null`) dates still pass, preserving the \"server's current date is used\" default. I also updated the field's description to document the rule.\n\n**Verification:** The new `errorRejectsFutureDate` acceptance test (posting `2999-01-01`) passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures) \u2014 the log confirms the future value is rejected with a `PastOrPresent` validation error before persistence.",
