    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change places the constraint exactly where a Spring/OpenAPI-generator codebase expects it. Since the model is generated from `openapi.yml`, the field-level `x-field-extra-annotation` is the idiomatic way to attach a Bean Validation constraint (`@PastOrPresent`) to the generated DTO field \u2014 there is no hand-written model class to edit, and adding it in the schema keeps the annotation co-located with the field's documentation.\n\n- The `@PastOrPresent` constraint is the natural, minimal expression of \"not later than the server's current date,\" and relying on the standard Bean Validation \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400 flow means no new controller/service logic is needed.\n- The prose description is updated alongside the constraint, so the schema stays self-documenting and consistent.\n- Nothing is duplicated and no class/method becomes a catch-all; the change is purely additive to the schema definition.",
